{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-57427",
  "enisaUuid": "fb21ff00-82ea-3138-b43d-e8c9bca48784",
  "description": "When kuma-dp is started against an HTTPS control plane and the operator did not pass a CA certificate, the data plane connects with TLS peer verification disabled, and the dataplane authentication token is sent over that unverified connection.\n\n\n\nAn on-path actor can intercept the dataplane authentication token and impersonate the control plane to the data plane, injecting a forged bootstrap configuration and taking over the proxy.",
